  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>According to the relation<br /><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi>E</mi><mo>∝</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>∝</mo><mi>υ</mi><mo>∝</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">L</mi></msub><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">=</mo></math>&nbsp;lower energy level</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;higher energy level<br /><br />In hydrogen atom the emission of the least energetic photon take place only when change in energy is minimum. This is possible for an electron that is present in <math><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math> and jumps to <math><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math> .</p>"
